WEBVTT

00:00:00.222 --> 00:00:03.987
Meet Qore: three Codex skills, adapted to your project.

00:00:03.987 --> 00:00:06.596
These are separate, actual runs.

00:00:08.222 --> 00:00:11.526
One profile captures the project's real commands and rules.

00:00:11.526 --> 00:00:17.943
It generates three specialized skills: planning, independent
review, and web UX.

00:00:20.222 --> 00:00:22.815
Five planning perspectives challenge the approach.

00:00:22.815 --> 00:00:28.897
The result separates keyboard access, the state we reach, and
where focus lands.

00:00:32.222 --> 00:00:37.074
Three reviewers and a fresh verifier reproduced four
coordination issues.

00:00:37.074 --> 00:00:42.445
Their fixes were checked separately, while the original
findings remain visible.

00:00:44.221 --> 00:00:49.025
The project manager, production agent, and reviewer exchanged
real messages.

00:00:49.025 --> 00:00:51.509
The delivery was accepted once.

00:00:51.509 --> 00:00:55.518
Sessions start manually; work was already in progress.

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:58.230
Now, the real Labs journey.

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:01.927
We open the first question without entering any answers.

00:01:05.222 --> 00:01:11.622
We reach help with the keyboard, open it with Enter, toggle it
with Space, and open it again.

00:01:11.622 --> 00:01:14.022
Each step has its own check.

00:01:20.222 --> 00:01:22.397
Closing help restores focus.

00:01:22.397 --> 00:01:25.592
Then Tab reaches Back.

00:01:27.222 --> 00:01:29.188
Enter returns to the introduction.

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:34.558
We check heading focus, the visible Start button, and the
unanswered state separately.

00:01:37.102 --> 00:01:38.817
This covers one desktop flow.

00:01:38.817 --> 00:01:41.201
The reports retain the evidence and limits.

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:43.811
Publication and application remain separate.
